{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c593","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7842-7623-9b92-35d8899ee7fd"},"sequence":292,"recorded_at":1780531400000579,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-2c57-7e61-97d5-49b9cf3e8459"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-2c57-7e61-97d5-49b9cf3e8459","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01e-2c57-7e61-97d5-49b9cf3e8459","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(7127 line(s) above)\n7128|### 11.2 RPC framing and handshake\n7129|\n7130|Mesh RPC uses line-delimited JSON, maximum line size 8 MiB, protocol\n7131|<code>urn:ax:protocol:rpc</code> version <code>2.0.0</code>. Binary chunk bytes\n7132|are unpadded base64url in the request body. Every request has a UUIDv7\n7133|<code>request_id</code>; every response echoes it.\n7134|\n7135|The first request MUST be <code>hello</code>:\n7136|\n7137|~~~json\n7138|{\n7139|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:rpc\",\n7140|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n7141|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-a070-7188-9172-1234567890ab\",\n7142|  \"operation\": \"hello\",\n7143|  \"body\": {\n7144|    \"host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n7145|    \"platform\": \"macos\",\n7146|    \"ax_version\": \"0.2.1\",\n7147|    \"nonce\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcA\",\n7148|    \"contracts\": {\n7149|      \"rpc\": [\"2.0.0\"],\n7150|      \"session_record\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7151|      \"session_event\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7152|      \"lease\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7153|      \"checkpoint\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7154|      \"workspace_group\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7155|      \"provider_identity\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7156|      \"blob\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7157|      \"transfer_manifest\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7158|      \"chunk\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7159|      \"materialization_plan\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7160|      \"tombstone\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7161|      \"tombstone_ack\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7162|      \"task_board_bundle\": [\"1.0.0\"]\n7163|    },\n7164|    \"max_line_bytes\": 8388608,\n7165|    \"max_object_bytes\": 5242880\n7166|  }\n7167|}\n7168|~~~\n7169|\n7170|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n7171|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code> UUIDv7,\n7172|<code>operation</code>, and the operation-specific <code>body</code>. The\n7173|<code>hello</code> body contains exactly the members shown. Its nonce is\n7174|unpadded base64url encoding of at least 128 random bits. The\n7175|<code>contracts</code> map contains exactly the fourteen displayed lower-snake-\n7176|case keys, each with a sorted, unique array of 1–16 Semantic Versions. These\n7177|are the immutable/wire contracts used by RPC object exchange. Configuration,\n7178|provider protocol/manifest/probe, task-board bridge, materialization recovery\n7179|state, Structured Error, Observation Event, and CLI Result MUST NOT appear in\n7180|this map. They are either local, carried by another protocol, or—in the error\n7181|case—statically embedded below.\n7182|\n7183|Normative <code>hello</code> success:\n7184|\n7185|~~~json\n7186|{\n7187|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:rpc\",\n7188|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n7189|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-a070-7188-9172-1234567890ab\",\n7190|  \"ok\": true,\n7191|  \"body\": {\n7192|    \"host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n7193|    \"platform\": \"linux\",\n7194|    \"ax_version\": \"0.2.1\",\n7195|    \"nonce\": \"cXJzdHV2d3h5ejAxMjM0NQ\",\n7196|    \"nonce_echo\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcA\",\n7197|    \"contracts\": {\n7198|      \"rpc\": [\"2.0.0\"],\n7199|      \"session_record\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7200|      \"session_event\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7201|      \"lease\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7202|      \"checkpoint\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7203|      \"workspace_group\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7204|      \"provider_identity\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7205|      \"blob\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7206|      \"transfer_manifest\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7207|      \"chunk\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7208|      \"materialization_plan\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7209|      \"tombstone\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7210|      \"tombstone_ack\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7211|      \"task_board_bundle\": [\"1.0.0\"]\n7212|    },\n7213|    \"max_line_bytes\": 8388608,\n7214|    \"max_object_bytes\": 5242880\n7215|  }\n7216|}\n7217|~~~\n7218|\n7219|The success body contains exactly the request identity/version/limit members,\n7220|the server's fresh <code>nonce</code>, and <code>nonce_echo</code> equal to the\n7221|request nonce. A success response contains exactly protocol, version, request\n7222|ID, <code>ok = true</code>, and body. A failure response substitutes\n7223|<code>ok = false</code> and one Structured Error and MUST omit body. Unknown\n7224|envelope or body members fail protocol 2.0.0.\n7225|\n7226|Mesh RPC protocol <code>2.x</code> statically binds every supported-major\n7227|failure envelope, including a rejected <code>hello</code>, to Structured Error\n7228|<code>1.0.0</code>. <code>error</code> is therefore deliberately absent from the\n7229|hello contracts map and is not independently negotiated on an RPC connection.\n7230|Section 15.1 defines the exact response-or-close behavior before handshake and\n7231|for an unsupported major.\n7232|\n7233|The server returns its own identity, nonce echo, supported contracts, and\n7234|limits. Peers negotiate the smaller line/object limit; protocol 2.0.0 requires\n7235|at least the values shown and MUST refuse a peer below them. The 5 MiB object\n7236|limit leaves room for base64url expansion and the response envelope below the\n7237|8 MiB line limit. Within a valid RPC-v2 hello, an absent required contract\n7238|returns the bound <code>incompatible_protocol</code> failure and closes. An\n7239|unsupported RPC major closes without a peer error frame and the initiator emits\n7240|that code locally, exactly as Section 15.1 requires. A peer MUST NOT\n7241|perform any other operation before a successful handshake.\n7242|\n7243|### 11.3 RPC operations\n7244|\n7245|Mesh RPC 2.0.0 operations are:\n7246|\n7247|| Operation | Purpose |\n7248|| --- | --- |\n7249|| <code>hello</code> | Authenticate configured identity and negotiate versions/limits |\n7250|| <code>health.get</code> | Read peer/service/provider health without payload contents |\n7251|| <code>inventory.roots</code> | Return Merkle roots and counts for record, event, manifest, tombstone, acknowledgement, and blob-ID sets |\n7252|| <code>inventory.children</code> | Expand one hexadecimal digest-prefix node |\n7253|| <code>objects.get</code> | Fetch immutable JSON/CBOR objects by digest |\n7254|| <code>transfer.begin</code> | Create or reopen staging for one manifest |\n7255|| <code>transfer.status</code> | Return verified object/chunk presence |\n7256|| <code>chunks.put</code> | Submit one base64url chunk with descriptor |\n7257|| <code>transfer.validate</code> | Assemble blobs and validate the complete manifest |\n7258|| <code>transfer.commit</code> | Atomically install immutable objects; does not materialize a workspace |\n7259|| <code>materialize.prepare</code> | Run destination conflict and capability checks |\n7260|| <code>materialize.commit</code> | Install a validated transaction in rollbackable prepared state (the historical operation name is retained) |\n7261|| <code>materialize.status</code> | Recover the exact durable materialization phase after a lost response or restart |\n7262|| <code>materialize.finalize</code> | Finalize a prepared transaction after dormant validation or winning-owner resume |\n7263|| <code>materialize.rollback</code> | Restore the pre-commit managed destination |\n7264|| <code>lease.refresh</code> | Exchange lease heads and return the deterministic winner |\n7265|| <code>tombstone.ack</code> | Persist a peer acknowledgement |\n7266|| <code>session.status</code> | Read authoritative lifecycle, process, checkpoint, and active-operation state for one session |\n7267|| <code>session.stop</code> | Execute the owner-side stop transaction in Section 13.9 |\n7268|| <code>handoff.prepare</code> | Reserve one graceful handoff against an expected source lease/checkpoint |\n7269|| <code>handoff.quiesce</code> | Quiesce the source and return its validated bulk-sync checkpoint |\n7270|| <code>handoff.stop</code> | Stop the source after destination validation and return any superseding closure checkpoint |\n7271|| <code>handoff.commit</code> | Persist the destination Lease Record on the source and park the old owner |\n7272|| <code>handoff.abort</code> | Abort a pre-lease handoff and explicitly unquiesce or retain stopped state |\n7273|\n7274|Every mutation body includes <code>initiator_host_id</code>; a session mutation\n7275|also includes an exact lease expectation. The receiver MUST revalidate both\n7276|immediately before mutation. These closed embedded types belong to Mesh RPC\n7277|2.0.0:\n7278|\n7279|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n7280|| --- | --- |\n7281|| <code>Namespace</code> | <code>record</code>, <code>event</code>, <code>manifest</code>, <code>tombstone</code>, <code>tombstone_ack</code>, or <code>blob</code> |\n7282|| <code>LeaseExpectation</code> | <code>epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n7283|| <code>LeaseHead</code> | <code>lease_record_id:digest</code> plus every <code>LeaseExpectation</code> member |\n7284|| <code>GroupMemberExpectation</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>winning_lease_record_id:digest</code>, <code>state:SessionState</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n7285|| <code>WorkspaceGroupExpectation</code> | <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_record_id:digest</code>, <code>observed_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>live_members:GroupMemberExpectation[1..1024]</code> |\n7286|| <code>MaterializationKind</code> | <code>workspace</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n7287|| <code>MaterializationIntent</code> | <code>passive_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n7288|| <code>MaterializationCohort</code> | <code>materialization_session_ids:sorted unique UUIDv7[1..1024]</code>, <code>ownership_transfer_session_ids:sorted unique UUIDv7[0..1024]</code> |\n7289|| <code>MaterializationSources</code> | <code>workspace_manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>task_board_bundle_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>derived_workspace_manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>fork_projection:ForkWorkspaceProjection&#124;null</code> |\n7290|| <code>WorkspaceMaterializationRequest</code> | <code>logical_root_mapping:map(string,absolute-path)[1..64]</code>, <code>destination:{logical_root:string[1..64],workspace_relative_path:path}</code>, <code>workspace_group_expectation:WorkspaceGroupExpectation</code>, <code>conflict_policy:fail&#124;copy&#124;worktree&#124;replace_managed_replica</code>, <code>replacement_confirmation_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n7291|| <code>VerifiedState</code> | <code>object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>, <code>blob_chunks:map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536]</code> |\n7292|| <code>WireObject</code> | <code>object_id:digest</code>, <code>media_type:application/json&#124;application/cbor</code>, <code>encoding:json&#124;cbor</code>, <code>data:base64url</code> |\n7293|| <code>SafeBoundary</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>evidence:provider_api&#124;provider_event&#124;managed_pty&#124;task_board_bridge&#124;accepted_test</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>store_stable:boolean</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique background_active&#124;database_handle_open&#124;input_not_blocked&#124;process_open&#124;provider_busy&#124;store_unstable[0..6]</code> |\n7294|| <code>ClosureEvidence</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n7295|| <code>ActiveOperation</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:stop&#124;graceful_handoff&#124;materialize</code>, <code>phase:string[1..64]</code>, <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n7296|| <code>DestinationClass</code> | <code>absent</code>, <code>empty</code>, <code>managed_unchanged</code>, <code>managed_divergent</code>, or <code>unmanaged_nonempty</code> |\n7297|| <code>MaterializationStatus</code> | <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>phase:unknown&#124;staging&#124;validating&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;rolling_back&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back&#124;failed</code>, <code>kind:MaterializationKind&#124;null</code>, <code>intent:MaterializationIntent&#124;null</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>destination_path:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>destination_classification:DestinationClass&#124;null</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code>, <code>destination_marker_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>provider_transaction_state:none&#124;unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;unknown&#124;not_started&#124;imported&#124;opened&#124;adopted&#124;resumed&#124;dormant_finalized&#124;rolled_back&#124;failed</code>, <code>task_board_manager_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>task_board_binding:AxBinding&#124;null</code>, <code>last_error_code:string[1..128]&#124;null</code> |\n7298|\n7299|<code>blob_chunks</code> object names are digest identifiers and its arrays are\n7300|sorted numeric indexes. Group members are sorted by session ID, contain every\n7301|current <code>live_members(G)</code> entry from Section 5.6 exactly once. A\n7302|WorkspaceGroupExpectation is only a fenced topology/state snapshot; it does\n7303|not itself select work or ownership changes.\n7304|\n7305|The MaterializationCohort makes those selections explicitly. Its\n7306|<code>materialization_session_ids</code> are the non-empty set whose checkpoint\n7307|workspace/provider/task-board state is installed by this transaction. Its\n7308|<code>ownership_transfer_session_ids</code> is a subset. It MUST be empty for\n7309|<code>passive_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, and <code>fork</code>,\n7310|and MUST be non-empty for <code>ownership_transfer</code>. The request's <code>session_id</code> is in\n7311|the materialization set and, for ownership transfer, in the transfer set. When\n7312|a workspace participates, both arrays are subsets of the expectation's live\n7313|members, except that a fork set contains exactly the fresh destination session\n7314|while its WorkspaceGroupExpectation describes the source group named by\n7315|<code>fork_projection</code>. A passive set may contain a stopped member and never authorizes\n7316|provider input, lease advance, adoption, or resume. Owner resume requires the\n7317|named session to be the already-winning stopped/failed owner and never advances\n7318|its lease. Ownership-transfer members may be\n7319|<code>running|idle|quiescing|checkpointing|stopped</code>; their non-null\n7320|managed-replica IDs, when present, identify the same shared destination on the\n7321|observed host. No implementation may infer a transfer cohort from the\n7322|materialization set or replace an empty transfer set with the current session.\n7323|Fork requires exactly one materialization session, a fresh epoch-1 destination\n7324|lease, and no ownership change to any source session.\n7325|\n7326|MaterializationSources and <code>workspace_request</code> form a closed tagged\n7327|union. <code>workspace</code> requires only a non-null workspace manifest and a\n7328|non-null workspace request. <code>provider</code> requires only a non-null\n7329|provider manifest and a null workspace request. <code>task_board</code>\n7330|requires only a non-null task-board bundle and a null workspace request.\n7331|<code>composite</code> requires a workspace manifest/request plus exactly one\n7332|of provider manifest or task-board bundle. Every other source member is\n7333|present as null. For every non-fork intent,\n7334|<code>derived_workspace_manifest_id</code> and <code>fork_projection</code> are\n7335|null. Fork requires both non-null: <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> is the\n7336|source group manifest in the selected Checkpoint closure and the derived ID is\n7337|the destination group manifest produced by the exact projection. All other\n7338|source IDs MUST be in the selected Checkpoint closure, and the generated\n7339|Materialization Plan kind and intent MUST equal the request.\n7340|\n7341|A safe boundary requires every idle/block/stability boolean true, both counts\n7342|zero, and empty blockers. Provider-plugin proof maps\n7343|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code>,\n7344|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n7345|<code>open_database_handles</code>, and its blocker names to the RPC registry;\n7346|BridgeSafeBoundary uses the Section 9.2 total mapping. In both mappings,\n7347|<code>store_stable</code> is true exactly when store generation is non-null and\n7348|<code>store_unstable</code> is absent. A safe RPC boundary additionally requires\n7349|non-null boundary and store-generation references; an unsafe diagnostic\n7350|boundary may carry either as null. Process handles are operation-local opaque values and MUST NOT be\n7351|persisted. In <code>MaterializationStatus</code>, phase\n7352|<code>unknown</code> requires null kind, intent, plan, checkpoint, destination,\n7353|classification, replica, marker, task-board manager/binding, and error, plus\n7354|provider and task-board transaction states <code>none</code>. Every other phase requires\n7355|non-null kind, intent, plan, and checkpoint. A workspace/composite status also\n7356|requires non-null destination path, classification, and managed-replica ID;\n7357|provider/task-board-only status requires all three null. Only a committed\n7358|workspace/composite status has a non-null destination marker. Prepared and\n7359|rolled-back phases require a null marker. Failed retains every known field and\n7360|a non-null error code. The provider transaction state is\n7361|<code>none</code> exactly when no provider manifest participates; it is\n7362|<code>unknown</code> only when that provider transaction was invoked but its\n7363|durable status has not been reconciled. Task-board transaction state is\n7364|<code>none</code> exactly when no Task-board Bundle participates and\n7365|<code>unknown</code> only after an attempted bridge mutation whose durable\n7366|result has not been reconciled. Its manager reference is non-null for\n7367|<code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, or\n7368|<code>dormant_finalized</code>; its binding is non-null only for adopted or\n7369|resumed. Neither is a control token. Operation bodies are exactly:\n7370|\n7371|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n7372|| --- | --- | --- |\n7373|| <code>health.get</code> | <code>{}</code> | <code>{service:ax, ax_version:semver, platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, observed_at:timestamp, degraded_codes:sorted unique string[0..1024]}</code> |\n7374|| <code>inventory.roots</code> | <code>{namespaces:sorted unique Namespace[1..6]}</code> | <code>{roots:sorted unique {namespace:Namespace,count:uint53,root_id:digest}[1..6]}</code> sorted by namespace |\n7375|| <code>inventory.children</code> | <code>{namespace:Namespace,prefix:lowercase-hex[0..64]}</code> | <code>{namespace:Namespace,prefix:lowercase-hex[0..64],count:uint53,node_hash:digest,children:sorted unique {label:hex-nibble,count:uint53,hash:digest}[0..16],ids:sorted unique digest[0..1]}</code> |\n7376|| <code>objects.get</code> | <code>{object_ids:sorted unique digest[1..4096],encodings:sorted unique json&#124;cbor[1..2]}</code> | <code>{objects:WireObject[1..4096]}</code> sorted by object ID |\n7377|| <code>transfer.begin</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest,transfer_id:UUIDv7&#124;null}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,expires_at:timestamp,verified:VerifiedState}</code> |\n7378|| <code>transfer.status</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,phase:receiving&#124;validating&#124;validated&#124;committed&#124;failed&#124;expired,verified:VerifiedState,last_error_code:string[1..128]&#124;null,expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n7379|| <code>chunks.put</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,transfer_id:UUIDv7,descriptor:Transfer Chunk Descriptor,data:base64url}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,chunk_id:digest,verified:boolean}</code> |\n7380|| <code>transfer.validate</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,transfer_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest,valid:boolean,verified_blob_count:uint53,verified_object_count:uint53,validation_summary_digest:digest}</code> |\n7381|| <code>transfer.commit</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,transfer_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest,validation_summary_digest:digest}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,installed_object_ids:sorted unique digest[1..65536],commit_marker_id:digest}</code> |\n7382|| <code>materialize.prepare</code> | Tagged <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation,checkpoint_id:digest,cohort:MaterializationCohort,sources:MaterializationSources,workspace_request:WorkspaceMaterializationRequest&#124;null}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,destination_path:absolute-path&#124;null,destination_classification:DestinationClass&#124;null,required_capabilities:sorted unique string[0..128],plan_id:digest,rollback_possible:boolean}</code> |\n7383|| <code>materialize.commit</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,plan_id:digest,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation}</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,phase:prepared,prepared_checkpoint_id:digest,destination_path:absolute-path&#124;null,destination_classification:DestinationClass&#124;null,managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,rollback_token:base64url-256+,provider_transaction_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;opened}</code> |\n7384|| <code>materialize.status</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>MaterializationStatus</code> |\n7385|| <code>materialize.finalize</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,rollback_token:base64url-256+,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation,activation:dormant_validated&#124;direct_owner_resumed&#124;task_board_owner_resumed,execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo&#124;null,profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null}</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,phase:committed,committed_checkpoint_id:digest,managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,destination_marker_id:digest&#124;null,provider_transaction_state:none&#124;committed,task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;resumed&#124;dormant_finalized,manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null,finalized_at:timestamp}</code> |\n7386|| <code>materialize.rollback</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,rollback_token:base64url-256+,reason:lease_lost&#124;validation_failed&#124;resume_failed&#124;operator_abort&#124;crash_recovery}</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,phase:rolled_back,rolled_back:boolean,restored_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,provider_transaction_state:none&#124;rolled_back,task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;rolled_back}</code> |\n7387|| <code>lease.refresh</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,known_lease_record_ids:sorted unique digest[0..4096]}</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,missing_leases:sorted unique Lease Record[0..4096],winner:LeaseHead,divergence:boolean}</code> |\n7388|| <code>tombstone.ack</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,acknowledgement:Tombstone Acknowledgement}</code> | <code>{tombstone_id:digest,ack_id:digest,stored:boolean}</code> |\n7389|| <code>session.status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,winner:LeaseHead,local_role:owner&#124;replica,state:SessionState,process_present:boolean,newest_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,active_operation:ActiveOperation&#124;null}</code> |\n7390|| <code>session.stop</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation,graceful:boolean,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,already_applied:boolean,closure:ClosureEvidence,final_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,resumable:boolean,bootstrap_aborted:boolean,resulting_state:stopped&#124;failed}</code> |\n7391|| <code>handoff.prepare</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,group_operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,expected_checkpoint_id:digest,destination_host_id:UUIDv7,workspace_group_expectation:WorkspaceGroupExpectation,cohort:MaterializationCohort}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,group_operation_id:UUIDv7,phase:reserved,source_lease:LeaseHead,source_checkpoint_id:digest,source_state:running&#124;idle&#124;stopped,workspace_group_expectation:WorkspaceGroupExpectation,cohort:MaterializationCohort,expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n7392|| <code>handoff.quiesce</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,safe_boundary:SafeBoundary,bulk_checkpoint_id:digest,manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024],source_phase:quiesced}</code> |\n7393|| <code>handoff.stop</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,destination_validation_summary_digest:digest}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,closure:ClosureEvidence,newest_checkpoint_id:digest,source_state:stopped}</code> |\n7394|| <code>handoff.commit</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,new_lease:Lease Record,destination_materialization_id:UUIDv7,plan_id:digest,committed_checkpoint_id:digest}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,winner:LeaseHead,source_role:replica,source_state:parked}</code> |\n7395|| <code>handoff.abort</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,recovery_mode:unquiesce&#124;remain_stopped}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,phase:aborted,resulting_source_state:running&#124;idle&#124;stopped}</code> |\n7396|\n7397|For <code>chunks.put</code>, success requires <code>verified = true</code>.\n7398|For <code>transfer.validate</code>, success requires <code>valid = true</code>.\n7399|For rollback and acknowledgement, success requires the corresponding boolean\n7400|true. A workspace request with replace policy requires a non-null\n7401|<code>replacement_confirmation_event_id</code>; every other policy requires\n7402|null. Every response uses the exact success/failure envelopes in Section 11.2.\n7403|\n7404|The caller MUST allocate <code>materialize.prepare.operation_id</code> and\n7405|<code>materialization_id</code> before the first request and MUST retain them\n7406|until the transaction is terminal. Before the first destination mutation, the\n7407|receiver MUST durably create the Materialization Journal with both IDs and a\n7408|digest of the complete canonical prepare body. The mutation idempotency key is\n7409|<code>(materialize.prepare, operation_id)</code>. An identical retry, including\n7410|after a lost response or receiver restart, returns the byte-identical recorded\n7411|success or failure and MUST NOT allocate a second journal, staging authority,\n7412|managed-replica ID, plan, or bridge operation ID. A changed canonical body,\n7413|including a changed materialization ID, is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and\n7414|causes no new mutation. <code>materialize.status</code> is an evolving read,\n7415|locates the one journal by caller-known <code>materialization_id</code>, uses the\n7416|RPC envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation, and MUST return the\n7417|current reconciled durable phase rather than replaying an earlier observation.\n7418|\n7419|The prepare response MUST echo the request kind and intent. For\n7420|workspace/composite it returns a non-null destination path, classification, and\n7421|managed-replica ID; for provider/task-board it returns all three as null.\n7422|Commit, status, finalize, and rollback MUST return the identical kind/intent\n7423|and preserve that nullability. A provider transaction ID/state is non-null/\n7424|non-<code>none</code> exactly when the selected provider plan has at least one\n7425|provider-store operation; a backend-identity validation-only plan has no\n7426|provider transaction. Task-board commit returns <code>opened</code> exactly\n7427|after the journaled import/open sequence and otherwise <code>none</code>.\n7428|<code>passive_replica</code> may finalize only with\n7429|<code>dormant_validated</code>; <code>owner_resume</code> and\n7430|<code>ownership_transfer</code> may finalize only with the direct or task-board\n7431|owner-resumed tag matching the Session Record after the expected lease proves\n7432|the destination is the winner. Fork uses the matching owner-resumed tag under\n7433|its fresh epoch-1 lease. Dormant validation requires null profile fields.\n7434|Either owner-resumed tag requires the exact effective profile and profile-\n7435|source event fixed by the activated session/checkpoint. For ordinary takeover\n7436|or owner resume this is the selected checkpoint pair. For fork it is the new\n7437|Session Record's projected creation profile with null new-session source; the\n7438|source checkpoint's nullable profile event remains only in\n7439|<code>fork.created.source_profile_event_id</code>.\n7440|A passive finalization MUST NOT start/adopt a provider, enable\n7441|input, or emit a lease event.\n7442|\n7443|Despite its retained operation name, <code>materialize.commit</code> ends in a\n7444|rollbackable <code>prepared</code> phase and MUST durably write the Section 10.6\n7445|journal before returning. It wraps any provider-plugin rollback token inside a\n7446|destination-local composite token; the plugin token never crosses RPC.\n7447|For a direct path the caller starts or resumes the provider, proves native\n7448|identity and process state, and then calls finalize with\n7449|<code>direct_owner_resumed</code>. For a task-board path, finalize itself uses\n7450|the durable Section 10.6 bridge IDs and token to adopt, resume, and prove status;\n7451|the caller MUST NOT perform those bridge mutations out of band.\n7452|<code>materialize.finalize</code> invokes provider\n7453|<code>materialize-commit</code> when applicable and removes host rollback bytes\n7454|only after the stated dormant or owner-resumed activation has been proved. For\n7455|a workspace/composite plan it writes the exact Section 10.6 Managed Replica\n7456|Marker before removing host rollback bytes and returns the same managed-replica\n7457|and marker IDs reported by <code>materialize.status</code>. Provider/task-board-\n7458|only plans return both IDs null. A marker write failure leaves the transaction\n7459|<code>committing</code> in the journal and retains rollback bytes.\n7460|<code>materialize.rollback</code> invokes provider rollback first, then the\n7461|task-board pre-adopt rollback/expiry procedure, then restores workspace bytes;\n7462|a failure in any layer leaves phase\n7463|<code>failed</code> and retains both recovery roots. Lost responses MUST be\n7464|recovered through <code>materialize.status</code>, never by guessing from a\n7465|destination directory.\n7466|\n7467|The RPC rollback reason maps unchanged to the provider operation when a\n7468|provider manifest participates:\n7469|\n7470|| RPC/journal cause | Provider rollback reason |\n7471|| --- | --- |\n7472|| Expected lease no longer wins before activation | <code>lease_lost</code> |\n7473|| Manifest, native discovery, board, workspace, or marker validation fails | <code>validation_failed</code> |\n7474|| Exact provider/task-board owner resume fails after prepare | <code>resume_failed</code> |\n7475|| Confirmed operator cancellation before activation | <code>operator_abort</code> |\n7476|| Restart reconciliation selects rollback | <code>crash_recovery</code> |\n7477|\n7478|No other mapping exists in Mesh RPC 2.0.0. The reason is persisted in the host\n7479|journal before the provider call and is part of both layers' idempotency input.\n7480|The required materialization fixtures are:\n7481|\n7482|| Fixture | Exact prepare selection | Required result/activation |\n7483|| --- | --- | --- |\n7484|| <code>MAT-WORKSPACE-STOPPED-SYNC</code> | <code>kind=workspace</code>, <code>intent=passive_replica</code>, one stopped session in materialization set, empty transfer set, workspace source/request only | Non-null path/classification/replica; dormant finalization; no process or lease change |\n7485|| <code>MAT-COMPOSITE-STOPPED-RESUME</code> | <code>kind=composite</code>, <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, already-winning stopped owner, empty transfer set, workspace plus provider source | Non-null path/classification/replica and provider transaction; exact owner resume before finalization; no new epoch |\n7486|| <code>MAT-PROVIDER-ONLY</code> | <code>kind=provider</code>, <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, provider source only, null workspace request | Null path/classification/replica/marker through every phase; provider transaction commits after owner resume |\n7487|| <code>MAT-TASK-BOARD-ONLY</code> | <code>kind=task_board</code>, <code>intent=passive_replica</code>, bundle source only, null workspace request | Null path/classification/replica/marker; imported/opened state remains dormant |\n7488|| <code>MAT-WORKSPACE-ONLY</code> | <code>kind=workspace</code>, <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, workspace source/request only | Non-null path/classification/replica/marker; provider transaction state remains <code>none</code> |\n7489|| <code>MAT-COMPOSITE-TAKEOVER</code> | <code>kind=composite</code>, <code>intent=ownership_transfer</code>, non-empty equal selected transfer cohort, workspace plus exactly one provider/bundle source | Prepare may precede fencing; owner-resumed finalization only after the destination lease wins |\n7490|\n7491|<code>MAT-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-STATUS</code> is the exact status projection after\n7492|commit/import/open and before adopt:\n7493|\n7494|~~~json\n7495|{\n7496|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n7497|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n7498|  \"kind\": \"task_board\",\n7499|  \"intent\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n7500|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:19bab2d797f2914ee4d452310e0a1a1d280859bf099e193bb5f1ccf2ebbb394f\",\n7501|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:59c2b9bd739552dc011bc956cbee83990a8ccbb4beb6ed2a230d77108f98e888\",\n7502|  \"destination_path\": null,\n7503|  \"destination_classification\": null,\n7504|  \"managed_replica_id\": null,\n7505|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n7506|  \"provider_transaction_state\": \"none\",\n7507|  \"task_board_transaction_state\": \"opened\",\n7508|  \"task_board_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n7509|  \"task_board_binding\": null,\n7510|  \"last_error_code\": null\n7511|}\n7512|~~~\n7513|\n7514|After successful owner finalize, the same object changes only\n7515|<code>phase=committed</code>, task-board state to <code>resumed</code>, manager\n7516|reference to the public adopted reference, and binding to the exact winning\n7517|session/epoch/lease. <code>MAT-TASK-BOARD-STATUS-N1</code> exposes an open token,\n7518|<code>N2</code> reports <code>opened</code> with a binding, and <code>N3</code>\n7519|reports <code>resumed</code> without one; all are invalid RPC results.\n7520|\n7521|<code>MAT-COHORT-N1</code> uses an empty transfer set with ownership-transfer\n7522|intent, <code>MAT-COHORT-N2</code> uses a non-empty transfer set with passive\n7523|intent, <code>MAT-KIND-N1</code> supplies a workspace request to provider-only,\n7524|and <code>MAT-KIND-N2</code> returns a managed-replica ID for task-board-only.\n7525|Each fails before mutation.\n7526|\n7527|Normative common failure response:\n7528|\n7529|~~~json\n7530|{\n7531|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:rpc\",\n7532|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n7533|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n7534|  \"ok\": false,\n7535|  \"error\": {\n7536|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:error\",\n7537|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n7538|    \"code\": \"lease_conflict\",\n7539|    \"message\": \"expected source lease is no longer the winner\",\n7540|    \"exit_code\": 10,\n7541|    \"retryable\": false,\n7542|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-06d0-77ee-8778-1234567890ab\",\n7543|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n7544|    \"details\": {}\n7545|  }\n7546|}\n7547|~~~\n7548|\n7549|Arrays with digest identities MUST be sorted bytewise and contain no duplicate.\n7550|<code>inventory.children</code> prefixes are 0–64 lowercase hexadecimal\n7551|characters; a receiver MUST reject a prefix outside that range. One\n7552|<code>objects.get</code> response MUST remain within the negotiated line limit;\n7553|the caller batches IDs accordingly.\n7554|\n7555|Every <code>session.*</code> and <code>handoff.*</code> mutation MUST be\n7556|accepted only from the configured destination/source host named by the active\n7557|operation and MUST revalidate the expected fencing token immediately before\n7558|each phase. One session MAY have at most one non-terminal graceful handoff.\n7559|For <code>handoff.prepare</code>, both cohort arrays MUST be non-empty and equal;\n7560|the current <code>session_id</code> MUST be a member. The receiver stores the\n7561|prepare-time WorkspaceGroupExpectation and cohort with the operation and\n7562|recomputes both before quiesce, stop, lease commit,\n7563|materialization finalization, and resume. Every per-session operation in one\n7564|whole-group takeover uses a distinct <code>operation_id</code> and the same\n7565|<code>group_operation_id</code>, destination, and expectation. No member lease\n7566|may advance until every migration-cohort member is safely stopped and prepared;\n7567|if any member fails or membership changes, all not-yet-fenced members abort and\n7568|all prepared destinations remain dormant. After the first member lease\n7569|advances, recovery MUST finish or explicitly recover every remaining cohort\n7570|member; it MUST NOT resume a stopped source member into the shared checkout.\n7571|Repeating a request with the same operation ID and canonical body returns the\n7572|recorded result; changing the body returns <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c595","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7842-7623-9b92-35d8899ee7fd"},"sequence":293,"recorded_at":1780531400000581,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-2c57-7e61-97d5-49b9cf3e8459"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-2c57-7e61-97d5-49b9cf3e8459","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b01e-2c57-7e61-97d5-49b9cf3e8459"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c597","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7842-7623-9b92-35d8899ee7fd"},"sequence":294,"recorded_at":1780531400000583,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01e27ce76a7bcbea47a05d6cdd9","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(7127 line(s) above)\n7128|### 11.2 RPC framing and handshake\n7129|\n7130|Mesh RPC uses line-delimited JSON, maximum line size 8 MiB, protocol\n7131|<code>urn:ax:protocol:rpc</code> version <code>2.0.0</code>. Binary chunk bytes\n7132|are unpadded base64url in the request body. Every request has a UUIDv7\n7133|<code>request_id</code>; every response echoes it.\n7134|\n7135|The first request MUST be <code>hello</code>:\n7136|\n7137|~~~json\n7138|{\n7139|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:rpc\",\n7140|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n7141|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-a070-7188-9172-1234567890ab\",\n7142|  \"operation\": \"hello\",\n7143|  \"body\": {\n7144|    \"host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n7145|    \"platform\": \"macos\",\n7146|    \"ax_version\": \"0.2.1\",\n7147|    \"nonce\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcA\",\n7148|    \"contracts\": {\n7149|      \"rpc\": [\"2.0.0\"],\n7150|      \"session_record\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7151|      \"session_event\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7152|      \"lease\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7153|      \"checkpoint\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7154|      \"workspace_group\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7155|      \"provider_identity\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7156|      \"blob\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7157|      \"transfer_manifest\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7158|      \"chunk\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7159|      \"materialization_plan\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7160|      \"tombstone\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7161|      \"tombstone_ack\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7162|      \"task_board_bundle\": [\"1.0.0\"]\n7163|    },\n7164|    \"max_line_bytes\": 8388608,\n7165|    \"max_object_bytes\": 5242880\n7166|  }\n7167|}\n7168|~~~\n7169|\n7170|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n7171|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code> UUIDv7,\n7172|<code>operation</code>, and the operation-specific <code>body</code>. The\n7173|<code>hello</code> body contains exactly the members shown. Its nonce is\n7174|unpadded base64url encoding of at least 128 random bits. The\n7175|<code>contracts</code> map contains exactly the fourteen displayed lower-snake-\n7176|case keys, each with a sorted, unique array of 1–16 Semantic Versions. These\n7177|are the immutable/wire contracts used by RPC object exchange. Configuration,\n7178|provider protocol/manifest/probe, task-board bridge, materialization recovery\n7179|state, Structured Error, Observation Event, and CLI Result MUST NOT appear in\n7180|this map. They are either local, carried by another protocol, or—in the error\n7181|case—statically embedded below.\n7182|\n7183|Normative <code>hello</code> success:\n7184|\n7185|~~~json\n7186|{\n7187|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:rpc\",\n7188|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n7189|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-a070-7188-9172-1234567890ab\",\n7190|  \"ok\": true,\n7191|  \"body\": {\n7192|    \"host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n7193|    \"platform\": \"linux\",\n7194|    \"ax_version\": \"0.2.1\",\n7195|    \"nonce\": \"cXJzdHV2d3h5ejAxMjM0NQ\",\n7196|    \"nonce_echo\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcA\",\n7197|    \"contracts\": {\n7198|      \"rpc\": [\"2.0.0\"],\n7199|      \"session_record\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7200|      \"session_event\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7201|      \"lease\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7202|      \"checkpoint\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7203|      \"workspace_group\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7204|      \"provider_identity\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7205|      \"blob\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7206|      \"transfer_manifest\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7207|      \"chunk\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7208|      \"materialization_plan\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7209|      \"tombstone\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7210|      \"tombstone_ack\": [\"1.0.0\"],\n7211|      \"task_board_bundle\": [\"1.0.0\"]\n7212|    },\n7213|    \"max_line_bytes\": 8388608,\n7214|    \"max_object_bytes\": 5242880\n7215|  }\n7216|}\n7217|~~~\n7218|\n7219|The success body contains exactly the request identity/version/limit members,\n7220|the server's fresh <code>nonce</code>, and <code>nonce_echo</code> equal to the\n7221|request nonce. A success response contains exactly protocol, version, request\n7222|ID, <code>ok = true</code>, and body. A failure response substitutes\n7223|<code>ok = false</code> and one Structured Error and MUST omit body. Unknown\n7224|envelope or body members fail protocol 2.0.0.\n7225|\n7226|Mesh RPC protocol <code>2.x</code> statically binds every supported-major\n7227|failure envelope, including a rejected <code>hello</code>, to Structured Error\n7228|<code>1.0.0</code>. <code>error</code> is therefore deliberately absent from the\n7229|hello contracts map and is not independently negotiated on an RPC connection.\n7230|Section 15.1 defines the exact response-or-close behavior before handshake and\n7231|for an unsupported major.\n7232|\n7233|The server returns its own identity, nonce echo, supported contracts, and\n7234|limits. Peers negotiate the smaller line/object limit; protocol 2.0.0 requires\n7235|at least the values shown and MUST refuse a peer below them. The 5 MiB object\n7236|limit leaves room for base64url expansion and the response envelope below the\n7237|8 MiB line limit. Within a valid RPC-v2 hello, an absent required contract\n7238|returns the bound <code>incompatible_protocol</code> failure and closes. An\n7239|unsupported RPC major closes without a peer error frame and the initiator emits\n7240|that code locally, exactly as Section 15.1 requires. A peer MUST NOT\n7241|perform any other operation before a successful handshake.\n7242|\n7243|### 11.3 RPC operations\n7244|\n7245|Mesh RPC 2.0.0 operations are:\n7246|\n7247|| Operation | Purpose |\n7248|| --- | --- |\n7249|| <code>hello</code> | Authenticate configured identity and negotiate versions/limits |\n7250|| <code>health.get</code> | Read peer/service/provider health without payload contents |\n7251|| <code>inventory.roots</code> | Return Merkle roots and counts for record, event, manifest, tombstone, acknowledgement, and blob-ID sets |\n7252|| <code>inventory.children</code> | Expand one hexadecimal digest-prefix node |\n7253|| <code>objects.get</code> | Fetch immutable JSON/CBOR objects by digest |\n7254|| <code>transfer.begin</code> | Create or reopen staging for one manifest |\n7255|| <code>transfer.status</code> | Return verified object/chunk presence |\n7256|| <code>chunks.put</code> | Submit one base64url chunk with descriptor |\n7257|| <code>transfer.validate</code> | Assemble blobs and validate the complete manifest |\n7258|| <code>transfer.commit</code> | Atomically install immutable objects; does not materialize a workspace |\n7259|| <code>materialize.prepare</code> | Run destination conflict and capability checks |\n7260|| <code>materialize.commit</code> | Install a validated transaction in rollbackable prepared state (the historical operation name is retained) |\n7261|| <code>materialize.status</code> | Recover the exact durable materialization phase after a lost response or restart |\n7262|| <code>materialize.finalize</code> | Finalize a prepared transaction after dormant validation or winning-owner resume |\n7263|| <code>materialize.rollback</code> | Restore the pre-commit managed destination |\n7264|| <code>lease.refresh</code> | Exchange lease heads and return the deterministic winner |\n7265|| <code>tombstone.ack</code> | Persist a peer acknowledgement |\n7266|| <code>session.status</code> | Read authoritative lifecycle, process, checkpoint, and active-operation state for one session |\n7267|| <code>session.stop</code> | Execute the owner-side stop transaction in Section 13.9 |\n7268|| <code>handoff.prepare</code> | Reserve one graceful handoff against an expected source lease/checkpoint |\n7269|| <code>handoff.quiesce</code> | Quiesce the source and return its validated bulk-sync checkpoint |\n7270|| <code>handoff.stop</code> | Stop the source after destination validation and return any superseding closure checkpoint |\n7271|| <code>handoff.commit</code> | Persist the destination Lease Record on the source and park the old owner |\n7272|| <code>handoff.abort</code> | Abort a pre-lease handoff and explicitly unquiesce or retain stopped state |\n7273|\n7274|Every mutation body includes <code>initiator_host_id</code>; a session mutation\n7275|also includes an exact lease expectation. The receiver MUST revalidate both\n7276|immediately before mutation. These closed embedded types belong to Mesh RPC\n7277|2.0.0:\n7278|\n7279|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n7280|| --- | --- |\n7281|| <code>Namespace</code> | <code>record</code>, <code>event</code>, <code>manifest</code>, <code>tombstone</code>, <code>tombstone_ack</code>, or <code>blob</code> |\n7282|| <code>LeaseExpectation</code> | <code>epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n7283|| <code>LeaseHead</code> | <code>lease_record_id:digest</code> plus every <code>LeaseExpectation</code> member |\n7284|| <code>GroupMemberExpectation</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>winning_lease_record_id:digest</code>, <code>state:SessionState</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n7285|| <code>WorkspaceGroupExpectation</code> | <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_record_id:digest</code>, <code>observed_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>live_members:GroupMemberExpectation[1..1024]</code> |\n7286|| <code>MaterializationKind</code> | <code>workspace</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>task_board</code>, or <code>composite</code> |\n7287|| <code>MaterializationIntent</code> | <code>passive_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, <code>ownership_transfer</code>, or <code>fork</code> |\n7288|| <code>MaterializationCohort</code> | <code>materialization_session_ids:sorted unique UUIDv7[1..1024]</code>, <code>ownership_transfer_session_ids:sorted unique UUIDv7[0..1024]</code> |\n7289|| <code>MaterializationSources</code> | <code>workspace_manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>task_board_bundle_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>derived_workspace_manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>fork_projection:ForkWorkspaceProjection&#124;null</code> |\n7290|| <code>WorkspaceMaterializationRequest</code> | <code>logical_root_mapping:map(string,absolute-path)[1..64]</code>, <code>destination:{logical_root:string[1..64],workspace_relative_path:path}</code>, <code>workspace_group_expectation:WorkspaceGroupExpectation</code>, <code>conflict_policy:fail&#124;copy&#124;worktree&#124;replace_managed_replica</code>, <code>replacement_confirmation_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n7291|| <code>VerifiedState</code> | <code>object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>, <code>blob_chunks:map(digest,sorted unique uint32[0..32768])[0..65536]</code> |\n7292|| <code>WireObject</code> | <code>object_id:digest</code>, <code>media_type:application/json&#124;application/cbor</code>, <code>encoding:json&#124;cbor</code>, <code>data:base64url</code> |\n7293|| <code>SafeBoundary</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>evidence:provider_api&#124;provider_event&#124;managed_pty&#124;task_board_bridge&#124;accepted_test</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>store_stable:boolean</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique background_active&#124;database_handle_open&#124;input_not_blocked&#124;process_open&#124;provider_busy&#124;store_unstable[0..6]</code> |\n7294|| <code>ClosureEvidence</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n7295|| <code>ActiveOperation</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>kind:stop&#124;graceful_handoff&#124;materialize</code>, <code>phase:string[1..64]</code>, <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n7296|| <code>DestinationClass</code> | <code>absent</code>, <code>empty</code>, <code>managed_unchanged</code>, <code>managed_divergent</code>, or <code>unmanaged_nonempty</code> |\n7297|| <code>MaterializationStatus</code> | <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>phase:unknown&#124;staging&#124;validating&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;rolling_back&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back&#124;failed</code>, <code>kind:MaterializationKind&#124;null</code>, <code>intent:MaterializationIntent&#124;null</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>destination_path:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>destination_classification:DestinationClass&#124;null</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code>, <code>destination_marker_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>provider_transaction_state:none&#124;unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;unknown&#124;not_started&#124;imported&#124;opened&#124;adopted&#124;resumed&#124;dormant_finalized&#124;rolled_back&#124;failed</code>, <code>task_board_manager_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>task_board_binding:AxBinding&#124;null</code>, <code>last_error_code:string[1..128]&#124;null</code> |\n7298|\n7299|<code>blob_chunks</code> object names are digest identifiers and its arrays are\n7300|sorted numeric indexes. Group members are sorted by session ID, contain every\n7301|current <code>live_members(G)</code> entry from Section 5.6 exactly once. A\n7302|WorkspaceGroupExpectation is only a fenced topology/state snapshot; it does\n7303|not itself select work or ownership changes.\n7304|\n7305|The MaterializationCohort makes those selections explicitly. Its\n7306|<code>materialization_session_ids</code> are the non-empty set whose checkpoint\n7307|workspace/provider/task-board state is installed by this transaction. Its\n7308|<code>ownership_transfer_session_ids</code> is a subset. It MUST be empty for\n7309|<code>passive_replica</code>, <code>owner_resume</code>, and <code>fork</code>,\n7310|and MUST be non-empty for <code>ownership_transfer</code>. The request's <code>session_id</code> is in\n7311|the materialization set and, for ownership transfer, in the transfer set. When\n7312|a workspace participates, both arrays are subsets of the expectation's live\n7313|members, except that a fork set contains exactly the fresh destination session\n7314|while its WorkspaceGroupExpectation describes the source group named by\n7315|<code>fork_projection</code>. A passive set may contain a stopped member and never authorizes\n7316|provider input, lease advance, adoption, or resume. Owner resume requires the\n7317|named session to be the already-winning stopped/failed owner and never advances\n7318|its lease. Ownership-transfer members may be\n7319|<code>running|idle|quiescing|checkpointing|stopped</code>; their non-null\n7320|managed-replica IDs, when present, identify the same shared destination on the\n7321|observed host. No implementation may infer a transfer cohort from the\n7322|materialization set or replace an empty transfer set with the current session.\n7323|Fork requires exactly one materialization session, a fresh epoch-1 destination\n7324|lease, and no ownership change to any source session.\n7325|\n7326|MaterializationSources and <code>workspace_request</code> form a closed tagged\n7327|union. <code>workspace</code> requires only a non-null workspace manifest and a\n7328|non-null workspace request. <code>provider</code> requires only a non-null\n7329|provider manifest and a null workspace request. <code>task_board</code>\n7330|requires only a non-null task-board bundle and a null workspace request.\n7331|<code>composite</code> requires a workspace manifest/request plus exactly one\n7332|of provider manifest or task-board bundle. Every other source member is\n7333|present as null. For every non-fork intent,\n7334|<code>derived_workspace_manifest_id</code> and <code>fork_projection</code> are\n7335|null. Fork requires both non-null: <code>workspace_manifest_id</code> is the\n7336|source group manifest in the selected Checkpoint closure and the derived ID is\n7337|the destination group manifest produced by the exact projection. All other\n7338|source IDs MUST be in the selected Checkpoint closure, and the generated\n7339|Materialization Plan kind and intent MUST equal the request.\n7340|\n7341|A safe boundary requires every idle/block/stability boolean true, both counts\n7342|zero, and empty blockers. Provider-plugin proof maps\n7343|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code>,\n7344|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n7345|<code>open_database_handles</code>, and its blocker names to the RPC registry;\n7346|BridgeSafeBoundary uses the Section 9.2 total mapping. In both mappings,\n7347|<code>store_stable</code> is true exactly when store generation is non-null and\n7348|<code>store_unstable</code> is absent. A safe RPC boundary additionally requires\n7349|non-null boundary and store-generation references; an unsafe diagnostic\n7350|boundary may carry either as null. Process handles are operation-local opaque values and MUST NOT be\n7351|persisted. In <code>MaterializationStatus</code>, phase\n7352|<code>unknown</code> requires null kind, intent, plan, checkpoint, destination,\n7353|classification, replica, marker, task-board manager/binding, and error, plus\n7354|provider and task-board transaction states <code>none</code>. Every other phase requires\n7355|non-null kind, intent, plan, and checkpoint. A workspace/composite status also\n7356|requires non-null destination path, classification, and managed-replica ID;\n7357|provider/task-board-only status requires all three null. Only a committed\n7358|workspace/composite status has a non-null destination marker. Prepared and\n7359|rolled-back phases require a null marker. Failed retains every known field and\n7360|a non-null error code. The provider transaction state is\n7361|<code>none</code> exactly when no provider manifest participates; it is\n7362|<code>unknown</code> only when that provider transaction was invoked but its\n7363|durable status has not been reconciled. Task-board transaction state is\n7364|<code>none</code> exactly when no Task-board Bundle participates and\n7365|<code>unknown</code> only after an attempted bridge mutation whose durable\n7366|result has not been reconciled. Its manager reference is non-null for\n7367|<code>opened</code>, <code>adopted</code>, <code>resumed</code>, or\n7368|<code>dormant_finalized</code>; its binding is non-null only for adopted or\n7369|resumed. Neither is a control token. Operation bodies are exactly:\n7370|\n7371|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n7372|| --- | --- | --- |\n7373|| <code>health.get</code> | <code>{}</code> | <code>{service:ax, ax_version:semver, platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, observed_at:timestamp, degraded_codes:sorted unique string[0..1024]}</code> |\n7374|| <code>inventory.roots</code> | <code>{namespaces:sorted unique Namespace[1..6]}</code> | <code>{roots:sorted unique {namespace:Namespace,count:uint53,root_id:digest}[1..6]}</code> sorted by namespace |\n7375|| <code>inventory.children</code> | <code>{namespace:Namespace,prefix:lowercase-hex[0..64]}</code> | <code>{namespace:Namespace,prefix:lowercase-hex[0..64],count:uint53,node_hash:digest,children:sorted unique {label:hex-nibble,count:uint53,hash:digest}[0..16],ids:sorted unique digest[0..1]}</code> |\n7376|| <code>objects.get</code> | <code>{object_ids:sorted unique digest[1..4096],encodings:sorted unique json&#124;cbor[1..2]}</code> | <code>{objects:WireObject[1..4096]}</code> sorted by object ID |\n7377|| <code>transfer.begin</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest,transfer_id:UUIDv7&#124;null}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,expires_at:timestamp,verified:VerifiedState}</code> |\n7378|| <code>transfer.status</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,phase:receiving&#124;validating&#124;validated&#124;committed&#124;failed&#124;expired,verified:VerifiedState,last_error_code:string[1..128]&#124;null,expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n7379|| <code>chunks.put</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,transfer_id:UUIDv7,descriptor:Transfer Chunk Descriptor,data:base64url}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,chunk_id:digest,verified:boolean}</code> |\n7380|| <code>transfer.validate</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,transfer_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest,valid:boolean,verified_blob_count:uint53,verified_object_count:uint53,validation_summary_digest:digest}</code> |\n7381|| <code>transfer.commit</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,transfer_id:UUIDv7,manifest_id:digest,validation_summary_digest:digest}</code> | <code>{transfer_id:UUIDv7,installed_object_ids:sorted unique digest[1..65536],commit_marker_id:digest}</code> |\n7382|| <code>materialize.prepare</code> | Tagged <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation,checkpoint_id:digest,cohort:MaterializationCohort,sources:MaterializationSources,workspace_request:WorkspaceMaterializationRequest&#124;null}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,destination_path:absolute-path&#124;null,destination_classification:DestinationClass&#124;null,required_capabilities:sorted unique string[0..128],plan_id:digest,rollback_possible:boolean}</code> |\n7383|| <code>materialize.commit</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,plan_id:digest,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation}</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,phase:prepared,prepared_checkpoint_id:digest,destination_path:absolute-path&#124;null,destination_classification:DestinationClass&#124;null,managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,rollback_token:base64url-256+,provider_transaction_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;opened}</code> |\n7384|| <code>materialize.status</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>MaterializationStatus</code> |\n7385|| <code>materialize.finalize</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,rollback_token:base64url-256+,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation,activation:dormant_validated&#124;direct_owner_resumed&#124;task_board_owner_resumed,execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo&#124;null,profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null}</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,phase:committed,committed_checkpoint_id:digest,managed_replica_id:UUIDv7&#124;null,destination_marker_id:digest&#124;null,provider_transaction_state:none&#124;committed,task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;resumed&#124;dormant_finalized,manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null,finalized_at:timestamp}</code> |\n7386|| <code>materialize.rollback</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,materialization_id:UUIDv7,rollback_token:base64url-256+,reason:lease_lost&#124;validation_failed&#124;resume_failed&#124;operator_abort&#124;crash_recovery}</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7,kind:MaterializationKind,intent:MaterializationIntent,phase:rolled_back,rolled_back:boolean,restored_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,provider_transaction_state:none&#124;rolled_back,task_board_transaction_state:none&#124;rolled_back}</code> |\n7387|| <code>lease.refresh</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,known_lease_record_ids:sorted unique digest[0..4096]}</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,missing_leases:sorted unique Lease Record[0..4096],winner:LeaseHead,divergence:boolean}</code> |\n7388|| <code>tombstone.ack</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,acknowledgement:Tombstone Acknowledgement}</code> | <code>{tombstone_id:digest,ack_id:digest,stored:boolean}</code> |\n7389|| <code>session.status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,winner:LeaseHead,local_role:owner&#124;replica,state:SessionState,process_present:boolean,newest_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,active_operation:ActiveOperation&#124;null}</code> |\n7390|| <code>session.stop</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_lease:LeaseExpectation,graceful:boolean,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,already_applied:boolean,closure:ClosureEvidence,final_checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null,resumable:boolean,bootstrap_aborted:boolean,resulting_state:stopped&#124;failed}</code> |\n7391|| <code>handoff.prepare</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,group_operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,expected_checkpoint_id:digest,destination_host_id:UUIDv7,workspace_group_expectation:WorkspaceGroupExpectation,cohort:MaterializationCohort}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,group_operation_id:UUIDv7,phase:reserved,source_lease:LeaseHead,source_checkpoint_id:digest,source_state:running&#124;idle&#124;stopped,workspace_group_expectation:WorkspaceGroupExpectation,cohort:MaterializationCohort,expires_at:timestamp}</code> |\n7392|| <code>handoff.quiesce</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,safe_boundary:SafeBoundary,bulk_checkpoint_id:digest,manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024],source_phase:quiesced}</code> |\n7393|| <code>handoff.stop</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,destination_validation_summary_digest:digest}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,closure:ClosureEvidence,newest_checkpoint_id:digest,source_state:stopped}</code> |\n7394|| <code>handoff.commit</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,new_lease:Lease Record,destination_materialization_id:UUIDv7,plan_id:digest,committed_checkpoint_id:digest}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,winner:LeaseHead,source_role:replica,source_state:parked}</code> |\n7395|| <code>handoff.abort</code> | <code>{initiator_host_id:UUIDv7,operation_id:UUIDv7,session_id:UUIDv7,expected_source_lease:LeaseExpectation,recovery_mode:unquiesce&#124;remain_stopped}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,phase:aborted,resulting_source_state:running&#124;idle&#124;stopped}</code> |\n7396|\n7397|For <code>chunks.put</code>, success requires <code>verified = true</code>.\n7398|For <code>transfer.validate</code>, success requires <code>valid = true</code>.\n7399|For rollback and acknowledgement, success requires the corresponding boolean\n7400|true. A workspace request with replace policy requires a non-null\n7401|<code>replacement_confirmation_event_id</code>; every other policy requires\n7402|null. Every response uses the exact success/failure envelopes in Section 11.2.\n7403|\n7404|The caller MUST allocate <code>materialize.prepare.operation_id</code> and\n7405|<code>materialization_id</code> before the first request and MUST retain them\n7406|until the transaction is terminal. Before the first destination mutation, the\n7407|receiver MUST durably create the Materialization Journal with both IDs and a\n7408|digest of the complete canonical prepare body. The mutation idempotency key is\n7409|<code>(materialize.prepare, operation_id)</code>. An identical retry, including\n7410|after a lost response or receiver restart, returns the byte-identical recorded\n7411|success or failure and MUST NOT allocate a second journal, staging authority,\n7412|managed-replica ID, plan, or bridge operation ID. A changed canonical body,\n7413|including a changed materialization ID, is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and\n7414|causes no new mutation. <code>materialize.status</code> is an evolving read,\n7415|locates the one journal by caller-known <code>materialization_id</code>, uses the\n7416|RPC envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation, and MUST return the\n7417|current reconciled durable phase rather than replaying an earlier observation.\n7418|\n7419|The prepare response MUST echo the request kind and intent. For\n7420|workspace/composite it returns a non-null destination path, classification, and\n7421|managed-replica ID; for provider/task-board it returns all three as null.\n7422|Commit, status, finalize, and rollback MUST return the identical kind/intent\n7423|and preserve that nullability. A provider transaction ID/state is non-null/\n7424|non-<code>none</code> exactly when the selected provider plan has at least one\n7425|provider-store operation; a backend-identity validation-only plan has no\n7426|provider transaction. Task-board commit returns <code>opened</code> exactly\n7427|after the journaled import/open sequence and otherwise <code>none</code>.\n7428|<code>passive_replica</code> may finalize only with\n7429|<code>dormant_validated</code>; <code>owner_resume</code> and\n7430|<code>ownership_transfer</code> may finalize only with the direct or task-board\n7431|owner-resumed tag matching the Session Record after the expected lease proves\n7432|the destination is the winner. Fork uses the matching owner-resumed tag under\n7433|its fresh epoch-1 lease. Dormant validation requires null profile fields.\n7434|Either owner-resumed tag requires the exact effective profile and profile-\n7435|source event fixed by the activated session/checkpoint. For ordinary takeover\n7436|or owner resume this is the selected checkpoint pair. For fork it is the new\n7437|Session Record's projected creation profile with null new-session source; the\n7438|source checkpoint's nullable profile event remains only in\n7439|<code>fork.created.source_profile_event_id</code>.\n7440|A passive finalization MUST NOT start/adopt a provider, enable\n7441|input, or emit a lease event.\n7442|\n7443|Despite its retained operation name, <code>materialize.commit</code> ends in a\n7444|rollbackable <code>prepared</code> phase and MUST durably write the Section 10.6\n7445|journal before returning. It wraps any provider-plugin rollback token inside a\n7446|destination-local composite token; the plugin token never crosses RPC.\n7447|For a direct path the caller starts or resumes the provider, proves native\n7448|identity and process state, and then calls finalize with\n7449|<code>direct_owner_resumed</code>. For a task-board path, finalize itself uses\n7450|the durable Section 10.6 bridge IDs and token to adopt, resume, and prove status;\n7451|the caller MUST NOT perform those bridge mutations out of band.\n7452|<code>materialize.finalize</code> invokes provider\n7453|<code>materialize-commit</code> when applicable and removes host rollback bytes\n7454|only after the stated dormant or owner-resumed activation has been proved. For\n7455|a workspace/composite plan it writes the exact Section 10.6 Managed Replica\n7456|Marker before removing host rollback bytes and returns the same managed-replica\n7457|and marker IDs reported by <code>materialize.status</code>. Provider/task-board-\n7458|only plans return both IDs null. A marker write failure leaves the transaction\n7459|<code>committing</code> in the journal and retains rollback bytes.\n7460|<code>materialize.rollback</code> invokes provider rollback first, then the\n7461|task-board pre-adopt rollback/expiry procedure, then restores workspace bytes;\n7462|a failure in any layer leaves phase\n7463|<code>failed</code> and retains both recovery roots. Lost responses MUST be\n7464|recovered through <code>materialize.status</code>, never by guessing from a\n7465|destination directory.\n7466|\n7467|The RPC rollback reason maps unchanged to the provider operation when a\n7468|provider manifest participates:\n7469|\n7470|| RPC/journal cause | Provider rollback reason |\n7471|| --- | --- |\n7472|| Expected lease no longer wins before activation | <code>lease_lost</code> |\n7473|| Manifest, native discovery, board, workspace, or marker validation fails | <code>validation_failed</code> |\n7474|| Exact provider/task-board owner resume fails after prepare | <code>resume_failed</code> |\n7475|| Confirmed operator cancellation before activation | <code>operator_abort</code> |\n7476|| Restart reconciliation selects rollback | <code>crash_recovery</code> |\n7477|\n7478|No other mapping exists in Mesh RPC 2.0.0. The reason is persisted in the host\n7479|journal before the provider call and is part of both layers' idempotency input.\n7480|The required materialization fixtures are:\n7481|\n7482|| Fixture | Exact prepare selection | Required result/activation |\n7483|| --- | --- | --- |\n7484|| <code>MAT-WORKSPACE-STOPPED-SYNC</code> | <code>kind=workspace</code>, <code>intent=passive_replica</code>, one stopped session in materialization set, empty transfer set, workspace source/request only | Non-null path/classification/replica; dormant finalization; no process or lease change |\n7485|| <code>MAT-COMPOSITE-STOPPED-RESUME</code> | <code>kind=composite</code>, <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, already-winning stopped owner, empty transfer set, workspace plus provider source | Non-null path/classification/replica and provider transaction; exact owner resume before finalization; no new epoch |\n7486|| <code>MAT-PROVIDER-ONLY</code> | <code>kind=provider</code>, <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, provider source only, null workspace request | Null path/classification/replica/marker through every phase; provider transaction commits after owner resume |\n7487|| <code>MAT-TASK-BOARD-ONLY</code> | <code>kind=task_board</code>, <code>intent=passive_replica</code>, bundle source only, null workspace request | Null path/classification/replica/marker; imported/opened state remains dormant |\n7488|| <code>MAT-WORKSPACE-ONLY</code> | <code>kind=workspace</code>, <code>intent=owner_resume</code>, workspace source/request only | Non-null path/classification/replica/marker; provider transaction state remains <code>none</code> |\n7489|| <code>MAT-COMPOSITE-TAKEOVER</code> | <code>kind=composite</code>, <code>intent=ownership_transfer</code>, non-empty equal selected transfer cohort, workspace plus exactly one provider/bundle source | Prepare may precede fencing; owner-resumed finalization only after the destination lease wins |\n7490|\n7491|<code>MAT-TASK-BOARD-OPENED-STATUS</code> is the exact status projection after\n7492|commit/import/open and before adopt:\n7493|\n7494|~~~json\n7495|{\n7496|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n7497|  \"phase\": \"prepared\",\n7498|  \"kind\": \"task_board\",\n7499|  \"intent\": \"ownership_transfer\",\n7500|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:19bab2d797f2914ee4d452310e0a1a1d280859bf099e193bb5f1ccf2ebbb394f\",\n7501|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:59c2b9bd739552dc011bc956cbee83990a8ccbb4beb6ed2a230d77108f98e888\",\n7502|  \"destination_path\": null,\n7503|  \"destination_classification\": null,\n7504|  \"managed_replica_id\": null,\n7505|  \"destination_marker_id\": null,\n7506|  \"provider_transaction_state\": \"none\",\n7507|  \"task_board_transaction_state\": \"opened\",\n7508|  \"task_board_manager_ref\": \"tbm:dormant:0198f4c8-7a10-7b22-8b3c-2234567890ab\",\n7509|  \"task_board_binding\": null,\n7510|  \"last_error_code\": null\n7511|}\n7512|~~~\n7513|\n7514|After successful owner finalize, the same object changes only\n7515|<code>phase=committed</code>, task-board state to <code>resumed</code>, manager\n7516|reference to the public adopted reference, and binding to the exact winning\n7517|session/epoch/lease. <code>MAT-TASK-BOARD-STATUS-N1</code> exposes an open token,\n7518|<code>N2</code> reports <code>opened</code> with a binding, and <code>N3</code>\n7519|reports <code>resumed</code> without one; all are invalid RPC results.\n7520|\n7521|<code>MAT-COHORT-N1</code> uses an empty transfer set with ownership-transfer\n7522|intent, <code>MAT-COHORT-N2</code> uses a non-empty transfer set with passive\n7523|intent, <code>MAT-KIND-N1</code> supplies a workspace request to provider-only,\n7524|and <code>MAT-KIND-N2</code> returns a managed-replica ID for task-board-only.\n7525|Each fails before mutation.\n7526|\n7527|Normative common failure response:\n7528|\n7529|~~~json\n7530|{\n7531|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:rpc\",\n7532|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n7533|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n7534|  \"ok\": false,\n7535|  \"error\": {\n7536|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:error\",\n7537|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n7538|    \"code\": \"lease_conflict\",\n7539|    \"message\": \"expected source lease is no longer the winner\",\n7540|    \"exit_code\": 10,\n7541|    \"retryable\": false,\n7542|    \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-06d0-77ee-8778-1234567890ab\",\n7543|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n7544|    \"details\": {}\n7545|  }\n7546|}\n7547|~~~\n7548|\n7549|Arrays with digest identities MUST be sorted bytewise and contain no duplicate.\n7550|<code>inventory.children</code> prefixes are 0–64 lowercase hexadecimal\n7551|characters; a receiver MUST reject a prefix outside that range. One\n7552|<code>objects.get</code> response MUST remain within the negotiated line limit;\n7553|the caller batches IDs accordingly.\n7554|\n7555|Every <code>session.*</code> and <code>handoff.*</code> mutation MUST be\n7556|accepted only from the configured destination/source host named by the active\n7557|operation and MUST revalidate the expected fencing token immediately before\n7558|each phase. One session MAY have at most one non-terminal graceful handoff.\n7559|For <code>handoff.prepare</code>, both cohort arrays MUST be non-empty and equal;\n7560|the current <code>session_id</code> MUST be a member. The receiver stores the\n7561|prepare-time WorkspaceGroupExpectation and cohort with the operation and\n7562|recomputes both before quiesce, stop, lease commit,\n7563|materialization finalization, and resume. Every per-session operation in one\n7564|whole-group takeover uses a distinct <code>operation_id</code> and the same\n7565|<code>group_operation_id</code>, destination, and expectation. No member lease\n7566|may advance until every migration-cohort member is safely stopped and prepared;\n7567|if any member fails or membership changes, all not-yet-fenced members abort and\n7568|all prepared destinations remain dormant. After the first member lease\n7569|advances, recovery MUST finish or explicitly recover every remaining cohort\n7570|member; it MUST NOT resume a stopped source member into the shared checkout.\n7571|Repeating a request with the same operation ID and canonical body returns the\n7572|recorded result; changing the body returns <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
