{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c663","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7842-7623-9b92-35d8899ee7fd"},"sequence":396,"recorded_at":1780531400000787,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-58ba-7681-ab9a-d52b58e8596f"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-58ba-7681-ab9a-d52b58e8596f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01e-58ba-7681-ab9a-d52b58e8596f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(15133 line(s) above)\n15134|## 17. Compatibility and migration\n15135|\n15136|### 17.1 Semantic-version rules\n15137|\n15138|Prepared specification v0.6.0 is a minor revision over immutable v0.5.0.\n15139|Section 6.6 and Section 11.10 define the new containing contracts and explicit\n15140|migration; every prior closed shape, fixture and release tag remains intact.\n15141|RPC 5 binds Error 1.3.0 without adding an error or hello-map key. This prepared\n15142|revision is not a statement that a v0.6.0 tag has been published.\n15143|\n15144|Each contract in Section 1.5 versions independently:\n15145|\n15146|- a major increment MAY break syntax or semantics and MUST require explicit\n15147|  negotiation/migration;\n15148|- a minor increment MAY add optional operations, enum values, or namespaced\n15149|  extension fields but MUST preserve all prior semantics;\n15150|- a patch increment MAY clarify constraints or fix a validator defect without\n15151|  adding a field or changing behavior.\n15152|\n15153|Specification package v0.5.0 is a minor release over v0.4.3 because it adds the\n15154|first-class TerminalBackend family and new independently versioned containing\n15155|contracts. Published v0.4.3 remains the exact immutable terminal-realm\n15156|baseline. It was a patch release over v0.4.2 that reconciled the\n15157|already approved roadmap, ownership/continuation semantics, complete Git\n15158|closure, and macOS execution-realm safety without adding or changing any\n15159|independently consumed wire member. Every contract active in v0.4.2 remained\n15160|unchanged in v0.4.3, including Structured Error 1.2.0; that release uses\n15161|existing codes with typed details. The independently versioned additions and\n15162|increments in v0.5.0 are exactly the Section 1.5 delta. Existing\n15163|v0.4.3, v0.4.2, and earlier tags remain immutable.\n15164|\n15165|Within any negotiated major version, new object data MUST live under a namespaced\n15166|<code>extensions</code> entry unless the consumer negotiated a newer minor\n15167|schema. Unknown top-level fields remain an error. Protocol peers choose the\n15168|highest mutually supported minor within a common major; they MUST NOT select a\n15169|major by coercion.\n15170|\n15171|Independent release versions do not override an explicit embedding rule.\n15172|Provider protocol and Mesh RPC major 2 and task-board bridge major 1 each bind\n15173|Structured Error 1.0.0 as Section 15.1 specifies. Provider Protocol 3, Mesh RPC\n15174|4, Terminal Backend Protocol 1, and CLI Result 4 bind Structured Error 1.3.0;\n15175|Directory/CLI/RPC 3 bindings to Error 1.2 remain exact. None negotiates the\n15176|error schema separately. Compatibility is evaluated first for the containing\n15177|protocol and then against its fixed embedded-error validator.\n15178|\n15179|The v0.2.0 correction is an explicit major-version boundary. Provider protocol\n15180|1.0.0, Mesh RPC 1.0.0, and Materialization recovery state 1.0.0 remain the\n15181|immutable v0.1.0 contracts and MUST NOT be interpreted using the corrected\n15182|2.0.0 request or journal shapes. There is no in-place migration of a live\n15183|machine-local 1.0.0 materialization transaction: upgrade MUST first reach a\n15184|safe terminal state or roll it back with the v0.1.0 implementation, then create\n15185|a new 2.0.0 transaction. A 2.0.0 peer or plugin rejects major 1 rather than\n15186|coercing its missing IDs or freezing an evolving status read.\n15187|\n15188|### 17.2 Reader/writer behavior\n15189|\n15190|A writer emits exactly the negotiated version. A reader:\n15191|\n15192|1. rejects an unsupported major;\n15193|2. accepts the same/lower supported minor;\n15194|3. preserves unknown namespaced extensions byte-for-byte when forwarding an\n15195|   immutable object;\n15196|4. rejects an unknown ownership/security enum that would affect behavior; and\n15197|5. MAY retain an unknown event as inert history but MUST NOT derive state from\n15198|   it.\n15199|\n15200|An <code>enabled = true</code> capability is valid only for the exact negotiated\n15201|contract and provider tuple or, for TerminalBackend capabilities, the exact\n15202|backend ID/implementation/protocol/generation/platform/OS evidence binding.\n15203|Version or binding mismatch changes it to conditional/unsupported and prevents\n15204|dependent activation.\n15205|\n15206|### 17.3 Immutable data migration\n15207|\n15208|Immutable objects MUST never be edited in place. A migration creates a new\n15209|schema-versioned object that references the prior object in\n15210|<code>extensions[\"works.relux.ax.migrated-from\"]</code>. That extension value is\n15211|a closed object containing exactly <code>schema_id:string</code>,\n15212|<code>schema_version:semver</code>, and <code>object_id:digest</code>. The writer\n15213|validates the new object and atomically advances a local reference. Old objects\n15214|remain available for rollback until retention policy allows collection.\n15215|\n15216|Configuration migration MUST create a backup, write a new file atomically, and\n15217|require <code>ax migrate config</code> for a major change. The CLI MUST NOT\n15218|silently rewrite a major-version config at startup.\n15219|\n15220|The derived SQLite index MAY be rebuilt at any time. It is never a migration\n15221|source of truth.\n15222|\n15223|### 17.4 Upgrade and downgrade\n15224|\n15225|Before upgrading, <code>ax</code> SHOULD checkpoint locally owned sessions.\n15226|After upgrade it MUST run schema/plugin/task-board compatibility checks before\n15227|auto-resume.\n15228|\n15229|A downgraded binary that cannot understand current records MUST enter\n15230|read-only diagnostic mode for those sessions. It MUST NOT resume, transfer\n15231|ownership, materialize, or write lower-version replacements.\n15232|\n15233|Provider upgrades invalidate prior tuple-specific acceptance until the adapter's\n15234|declared version range and compatibility fixture cover the new version. Muse\n15235|and Antigravity unknowns in Section 8 remain explicit version gates.\n15236|\n15237|TerminalBackend upgrade negotiates Manifest, Probe, Protocol, Provider,\n15238|Configuration, Event, CLI Result, and Error versions independently. A peer that\n15239|cannot activate the backend contract MAY still browse and synchronize sanitized\n15240|immutable evidence; it MUST report activation unavailable rather than omit the\n15241|Session. Restore binds the previously selected backend and generation, while a\n15242|new owner activation may select another admitted backend. Downgrade is read-only\n15243|for every unrepresentable binding or ID and never emits a lower-version\n15244|replacement.\n15245|\n15246|### 17.5 Directory release compatibility\n15247|\n15248|AX/spec v0.4.0 introduced Directory Node/records/query at 1.0.0, Mesh RPC 3.0.0,\n15249|Configuration 2.0.0, CLI Result 3.0.0, Session Record/Event 3.0.0, and\n15250|Structured Error 1.2.0. Observation Event remains 1.0.0 because its event name\n15251|is an open grammar and its object shape is unchanged. Provider Protocol remains\n15252|2.0.0; Directory Node is its separately negotiated companion. Session Adapter,\n15253|all v0.3 clone schemas, Materialization Plan 1/2, Journal 2/3, Checkpoint,\n15254|Provider Identity, Workspace Group, Blob/Chunk/Transfer, lease, terminal, and\n15255|tombstone contracts are reused unchanged.\n15256|\n15257|AX/spec v0.4.1 is a patch errata over that publication. It adds no field,\n15258|operation, outcome, namespace, or authority and retains every Section 1.5\n15259|contract version. It resolves combinations that were already impossible under\n15260|the stronger global rules: direct unmanaged move cannot satisfy AX lease/event\n15261|requirements; response and query correlation obey their existing tags and\n15262|array positions; the two enrichment generator discriminators must agree; and a\n15263|lineage projection identifies which existing member supplies its singular\n15264|display fields. Those changes are compatibility-neutral constraint\n15265|clarifications and fixture corrections under Section 17.1. However, v0.4.1\n15266|also changed the closed Directory Node Request 1.0.0\n15267|<code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary while retaining its version. That\n15268|change is not compatible and MUST NOT be used as Request 1.0.0 implementation\n15269|evidence.\n15270|\n15271|AX/spec v0.4.2 corrects that post-publication defect without moving either\n15272|prior tag. Directory Node Protocol 1.0.0 and Request 1.0.0 retain the exact\n15273|published v0.4.0 vocabulary <code>darwin|linux|windows</code>. Directory Node\n15274|Protocol 2.0.0 and Request 2.0.0 introduce the AX vocabulary\n15275|<code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>. Manifest 1.0.0 and Response 1.0.0 remain\n15276|shape-compatible and are bound explicitly by both protocol majors. v0.4.2 also\n15277|strengthens conformance validation without changing directory object bytes:\n15278|common digests, UUIDv4/UUIDv7 values, timestamps, tagged unions, nullable\n15279|members, and sorted-unique arrays are checked by schema/path rules; timestamp\n15280|validation includes real calendar validity. v0.4.0 and v0.4.1 remain immutable\n15281|history, but v0.4.2 is the first safe Directory implementation baseline.\n15282|\n15283|RPC 3 and RPC 2 are dual-stack for at least one stable release. Config 2 has\n15284|the explicit backup/atomic migration and read-only downgrade behavior in\n15285|Section 6.4. CLI Result 1/2 and Session Record/Event 1/2 remain readable and\n15286|immutable. A v3 writer never inserts directory/adoption members into those\n15287|closed older objects. Unsupported majors, unknown closed fields/tags, tuple\n15288|revocation, or contradictory façade manifests fail closed.\n15289|\n15290|Environment tuple admission remains the signed v0.3 registry. Directory\n15291|discovery may report a safe degraded source read, but preview/head/adoption/\n15292|native clone/write/launch require the exact separately admitted capability.\n15293|One environment module backs Provider 2, Session Adapter 1, and Directory Node\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
