{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c80f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7842-7623-9b92-35d8899ee7fd"},"sequence":610,"recorded_at":1780531400001215,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01ee48f76ba9c07be04a6dace38","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-16-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"cataloggen -adopted\\\\|adopted.*check\\\\|validation suite\\\\|26-command\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.json\\\" --include=\\\"*.sh\\\" . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\".task-board/\\\" | grep -v node_modules | head -20; echo ===; ls .planning/ 2>/dev/null; ls scripts/ 2>/dev/null\",\n  \"description\": \"Find validation suite definition\",\n  \"exit_code\": 1,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"failed\",\n  \"terminal_reason\": \"process exited with status 1\",\n  \"scan_scope_hint\": \"[hint] unscoped recursive scan over the workspace root — scope the next search to the subtree the task names or use the bounded search tool; if this scan backgrounded, harvest or terminate it before ending the turn.\",\n  \"output\": \"./LOGBOOK.md:160:- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \\\".\\\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:161:- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\\n./task-board.config.json:426:          \\\"go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\\",\\n./internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md:394:| Managed replica | A destination path created or explicitly adopted by <code>ax</code>, with a recorded last-materialized checkpoint. |\\n./internal/specdoc/SPEC.md:378:| Managed replica | A destination path created or explicitly adopted by <code>ax</code>, with a recorded last-materialized checkpoint. |\\n./README.md:3032:go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n./README.md:3037:adopted release, so the check stays valid when the adopted release changes.\\n./README.md:3369:| Go toolchain | Verify global and assigned-scope specification ownership, validate versioned Configuration readers/current writer, validate owner-local storage, immutable installs, and SQLite rebuild/recovery, validate and fuzz common wire scalars, canonical identities, core records, Session Events, and Observation Events, validate the Structured Error registry, its static containing-contract bindings, and its detail redaction, validate the CLI Result envelopes, command bodies, common flags, rendering boundary, and exit-status mapping, classify one completed `ax --json` invocation from stdout and its exit status through the machine reader and replay the frozen historical envelope corpora, generate and check the typed catalogs, build, test, and measure the Go implementation | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck`; `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2` (every other assigned section is refused with its measured coverage ratio); `go test ./internal/config -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/localstore -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/scalar -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/scalar -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/axerror -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/cliresult -cover -count=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzClosedIdentityShapeRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObservationEventRefusal$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`; `go generate ./internal/catalog`; `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` (`-metadata`/`-contracts` select the same inputs explicitly); `go test ./... -v`; `go test ./... -cover`; `go build ./...` | Read-only traceability report; owner-only roots, immutable blob/quarantine data, and `<state>/index.sqlite` plus recovery evidence only when storage entries are called; `internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go`; Go build/fuzz cache; test output captured under `.temp/<TASK-ID>/` when needed |\\n===\\n260829_024701_epic-260829-dz9yvx.md\\n260830_020530_project.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-1ewjla.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-1uwj54.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-27bix9.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-391tge.md\\n260830_020537_epic-260830-3v9jlg.md\\n260830_020538_task-260830-55kcni.md\\n260830_021436_epic-260830-37rgqn.md\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4357,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1090,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"failure"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c811","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7842-7623-9b92-35d8899ee7fd"},"sequence":611,"recorded_at":1780531400001217,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01eeb8d742faf5e41a893f82d33","text":"Read text file `internal/hosttrust/authorize.go`.\n1|package hosttrust\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"errors\"\n6|\t\"fmt\"\n7|\t\"time\"\n8|\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n10|)\n11|\n12|// AuthRequest carries one dispatch or mutation-boundary authorization check.\n13|// SnapshotGeneration binds the stream to the coherent snapshot it was opened\n14|// under; LocalCredentialID and the remote DER bytes select the exact enrolled\n15|// entries; Allowlisted is the local mesh allowlist; HelloHostID is the\n16|// authenticated hello identity; ExpectedRemoteHostID is the selected\n17|// configured destination on the client.\n18|type AuthRequest struct {\n19|\tSnapshotGeneration   uint64\n20|\tLocalHostID          string\n21|\tLocalCredentialID    string\n22|\tRemoteLeafDER        []byte\n23|\tRemoteRootDER        []byte\n24|\tExpectedRemoteHostID string\n25|\tAllowlisted          []string\n26|\tHelloHostID          string\n27|\tNow                  time.Time\n28|}\n29|\n30|// Formatting an authorization request must never expose DER bytes, UUIDs,\n31|// digests or allowlists.\n32|func (AuthRequest) String() string   { return \"host channel authorization request\" }\n33|func (AuthRequest) GoString() string { return \"host channel authorization request\" }\n34|func (AuthRequest) Format(state fmt.State, verb rune) {\n35|\t_, _ = state.Write([]byte(\"host channel authorization request\"))\n36|}\n37|\n38|// Formatting a snapshot must never expose the entries it binds.\n39|func (Snapshot) String() string   { return \"host trust snapshot\" }\n40|func (Snapshot) GoString() string { return \"host trust snapshot\" }\n41|func (Snapshot) Format(state fmt.State, verb rune) {\n42|\t_, _ = state.Write([]byte(\"host trust snapshot\"))\n43|}\n44|\n45|// AuthorizeDispatch checks current generation, local credential validity,\n46|// allowlist membership and authenticated hello against one committed read\n47|// held under the shared authorization lock. The check observes a coherent\n48|// snapshot, but the dispatch itself runs after the lock releases, so the\n49|// caller must bind the admitted generation to the stream and enforce the\n50|// one-second invalidation on commit: re-check currency before sending, and\n51|// close stale-generation streams on watchdog, never on notifications alone.\n52|// Mutation side effects additionally require WithMutationAuthorization, which\n53|// holds the exclusive lock across the recheck and the boundary. Work prepared\n54|// under an old generation cannot gain new authority by refreshing a cached\n55|// number: a stale snapshot refuses.\n56|func (store *Store) AuthorizeDispatch(snapshot Snapshot, request AuthRequest) error {\n57|\t// Pending joint intent converges before the currency check, so a\n58|\t// dispatch bound before a crash compares against the recovered\n59|\t// generation and refuses stale instead of admitting superseded trust.\n60|\t// Convergence failures name their own operation and pass through: a\n61|\t// refused recovery is a durability event, not an authorization verdict.\n62|\tunlock, err := lockForConvergedRead(store.fs, store.root, store.lock, store.paths)\n63|\tif err != nil {\n64|\t\treturn err\n65|\t}\n66|\tdefer unlock()\n67|\tcurrent, err := readCommitted(store)\n68|\tif err != nil {\n69|\t\treturn err\n70|\t}\n71|\t// The stream binding must match the snapshot it was opened under: work\n72|\t// prepared under an old generation cannot gain new authority by\n73|\t// refreshing a cached number.\n74|\tif request.SnapshotGeneration != snapshot.Generation {\n75|\t\treturn trustError(TrustError{Operation: \"authorize generation\", Err: ErrStaleGeneration})\n76|\t}\n77|\tif snapshot.Generation != current.Generation {\n78|\t\treturn trustError(TrustError{Operation: \"authorize generation\", Err: ErrStaleGeneration})\n79|\t}\n80|\treturn checkAuthorization(snapshot.Trust, request)\n81|}\n82|\n83|// readCommitted reads the committed trust without acquiring the lock: the\n84|// caller must already hold the authorization lock and have converged\n85|// pending joint intent, so the read nests safely inside a holder instead\n86|// of blocking on it.\n87|func readCommitted(store *Store) (TrustStore, error) {\n88|\tpath := store.TrustPath()\n89|\tinfo, err := store.fs.Lstat(path)\n90|\tif err != nil {\n91|\t\treturn TrustStore{}, trustError(TrustError{Operation: \"authorize generation\", Err: errors.Join(ErrAuthorizationRefused, err)})\n92|\t}\n93|\tif err := verifyOwnerFile(path, info, 0o600); err != nil {\n94|\t\treturn TrustStore{}, err\n95|\t}\n96|\tdocument, err := store.fs.ReadFile(path)\n97|\tif err != nil {\n98|\t\treturn TrustStore{}, trustError(TrustError{Operation: \"authorize generation\", Err: errors.Join(ErrAuthorizationRefused, err)})\n99|\t}\n100|\tcommitted, err := DecodeTrust(document)\n101|\tif err != nil {\n102|\t\treturn TrustStore{}, err\n103|\t}\n104|\treturn committed, nil\n105|}\n106|\n107|func checkAuthorization(trust TrustStore, request AuthRequest) error {\n108|\tconst operation = \"authorize dispatch\"\n109|\tlocal, found := findEntry(trust, request.LocalCredentialID)\n110|\tif !found {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
