{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-7842-7623-9b92-35d8899ee7fd"},"sequence":715,"recorded_at":1780531400001425,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0ef4e50a-8dbf-492d-ac24-c7f49d0e006b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b021-6c4d-72b2-86d4-a266d6c896d8"},"task_id":"01a0b021-6c4d-72b2-86d4-a266d6c896d8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b021-6c4d-72b2-86d4-a266d6c896d8","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(14859 line(s) above)\n14860|unknown code retains the envelope's exit class and MUST NOT be interpreted as\n14861|success.\n14862|\n14863|The v0.4.3 realm and route constraints add no error code. Missing or unsafe\n14864|broker/server-generation/functional-sentinel evidence uses\n14865|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed details containing\n14866|<code>capability</code>, <code>caller_realm</code>,\n14867|<code>broker_state</code>, <code>tmux_server_generation</code>, and\n14868|<code>remediation</code>. A missing or failed provider-auth smoke uses\n14869|<code>target_auth_missing</code> with typed <code>provider_id</code>,\n14870|<code>provider_build</code>, <code>macos_version</code>,\n14871|<code>tmux_server_generation</code>, and <code>remediation</code>. Route choice\n14872|continues to use <code>interactive_choice_required</code>. Implementations MUST\n14873|NOT mint a realm-specific code while these existing codes remain truthful.\n14874|\n14875|Structured Error 1.2.0 retains the exact 1.1 shape and all prior codes. It is\n14876|bound by Directory Node 1 and 2, Mesh RPC 3, CLI Result 3, and Directory Query 1 and\n14877|adds the exact mappings below:\n14878|\n14879|| Exit | Directory codes |\n14880|| ---: | --- |\n14881|| 2 | <code>directory_instance_not_found</code>, <code>directory_instance_ambiguous</code>, <code>query_invalid</code> |\n14882|| 3 | <code>inventory_stale</code>, <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> |\n14883|| 4 | <code>host_offline</code> |\n14884|| 6 | <code>directory_mesh_unsupported</code>, <code>continuation_route_unavailable</code>, <code>adoption_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_attach_unavailable</code> |\n14885|| 7 | <code>field_forbidden</code>, <code>target_auth_missing</code> |\n14886|| 9 | <code>observation_gap</code>, <code>observation_conflict</code>, <code>adapter_protocol_violation</code> |\n14887|| 10 | <code>lineage_ambiguous</code>, <code>annotation_conflict</code> |\n14888|| 12 | <code>operation_uncertain</code> |\n14889|| 13 | <code>enrichment_model_unavailable</code> |\n14890|| 15 | <code>cloned_source_still_active</code> |\n14891|| 16 | <code>instance_identity_weak</code>, <code>preview_policy_blocked</code>, <code>enrichment_policy_blocked</code>, <code>enrichment_head_changed</code>, <code>continuation_plan_stale</code>, <code>unmanaged_remote_forbidden</code>, <code>workspace_route_conflict</code>, <code>cloning_fidelity_unacceptable</code>, <code>operation_in_progress</code> |\n14892|\n14893|Directory codes reuse an earlier identical core code where listed in both\n14894|registries; their meaning is unchanged. <code>operation_uncertain</code> is not\n14895|retry permission: status/recovery inspection is mandatory. Partial target-first\n14896|move uses the successful/partial outcome and exit 15 without pretending the\n14897|target failed.\n14898|\n14899|For Directory Node 1, Directory Node 2, and RPC 3, a syntactically valid\n14900|supported-major request receives one failure envelope with Error 1.2. The sole\n14901|unsupported-major exception is a fresh Directory Node <code>manifest</code>\n14902|bootstrap attempt, which uses the exact downgrade response/exit tuple in\n14903|Section 7.9. Every other unsupported major, unparseable/oversize first frame,\n14904|missing framing identity, or response that cannot be framed causes\n14905|close/termination without trusting a peer/child error; the caller emits a local\n14906|1.2 <code>incompatible_protocol</code> or\n14907|<code>adapter_protocol_violation</code>/<code>transport_failure</code> as\n14908|applicable. Error is a static binding and never a hello-contract key.\n14909|\n14910|#### Structured Error 1.3.0 TerminalBackend codes\n14911|\n14912|Structured Error 1.3.0 retains the exact 1.2 top-level shape and every 1.0–1.2\n14913|code-to-exit mapping. It changes only <code>schema_version</code> to exact\n14914|<code>1.3.0</code> and adds these literal codes:\n14915|\n14916|| Exit | TerminalBackend codes |\n14917|| ---: | --- |\n14918|| 4 | <code>terminal_backend_not_found</code>, <code>terminal_backend_ambiguous</code> |\n14919|| 6 | <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code> |\n14920|| 7 | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code> |\n14921|| 9 | <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> |\n14922|| 10 | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code> |\n14923|| 13 | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code> |\n14924|\n14925|<code>terminal_backend_not_found</code> is valid only after a complete valid\n14926|registry/discovery read; a partial, failed, or malformed read is\n14927|<code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code>.\n14928|<code>terminal_backend_ambiguous</code> covers duplicate IDs or more than one\n14929|trusted implementation resolving the same ID and never selects one by order.\n14930|Unknown ID and known-but-unavailable implementation remain distinct.\n14931|<code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code> covers missing, expired,\n14932|self-minted, contradictory, or wrong-binding evidence.\n14933|<code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code> covers policy/default attempts to\n14934|replace the persisted restore backend. <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
